│ women and by the standard procedure in 1,402 women. Women in the fibrin sealant group were significantly older. The  │
│ pregnancy rate was not significantly different between the groups in the whole-cohort study (20.4% versus 23.1%),    │
│ but it was significantly higher in the fibrin sealant group in the case-control study (25.3% versus 14.9%). This     │
│ also was true when the older women (>35 years) and the women with > or =4 previous failed IVF attempts were analyzed │
